```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: No one. The operating point (long, slow-streaming, front-loaded, truncation-resistant tool results where rho>=1) does not occur in real agent tool traffic. Gate EXP-0038 measured N=1641 real records across 5 classes (api_json, code_exec_log, db_query, web_search, search_rag): median rho 0.007-0.508, 0-9% clear rho>=1. The lone high-rho class (search_rag, artificial 1274-tok HotpotQA distractor) collapses to 0% clearing rho>=1 under realistic reasoning next-step (N_step=64-256). Real tool results are 46-225 tokens — prefill completes in sub-100ms on H100, faster than the next decode step.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only artifact. EXP-0037's favorable break-even was correct math over an unreal operating point (rho>=2, long slow-streaming front-loaded results). Production agent stacks (vLLM/TGI/SGLang) already use incremental-prefill: tokens stream into KV cache continuously as they arrive, not wait-for-EOF. The addressable latency (residual gap between last-token-arrival and next-step-need) is largely already overlapped. Dumb-truncation @N=512 captures 100% actionable content for 4/5 classes (api/code/db/web) — a parameter-free baseline is already correct everywhere rho is low.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Empirically empty regime: rho>=1 occurs in 0-9% of real cases, 0% under realistic next-step; Adversarial bind: the only class with rho>=1 (search_rag) is also the only non-end-front-loaded (5.5% actionable-end <=0.3) and truncation-resistant (0-14.5%), so early-commit would be wrong exactly where it has time to act; Production baseline already wins: incremental-prefill overlaps the same latency without correctness risk or detector complexity; Prior art covers the latency: LLMCompiler (Kim et al. 2023, arXiv:2312.04511) captures inter-call latency via call-graph parallelism, lossless, no redo penalty; No measurable win: for 46-225 tok results, prefill is ~instant vs decode, nothing meaningful to overlap]
RATIONALE: Gate EXP-0038 fired kill criteria on two independent measures: (1) rho < 1 for dominant classes (median 0.007-0.508; 0% clear rho>=1 for api_json, code_exec_log, db_query, web_search; search_rag collapses to 0% under realistic N_step), and (2) dumb-truncation @512 fully captures actionable content for 4/5 classes (100%/100%/100%/100%). The adversarial (f_fl, rho) correlation is confirmed: search_rag is the only high-rho class and the only non-end-front-loaded (5.5% vs 61-93% for others) and truncation-resistant (0-14.5% vs 100%). Production incremental-prefill (vLLM/TGI/SGLang) streams tokens into KV continuously, overlapping sub-100ms prefill for 46-225 tok results. Prior art LLMCompiler (arXiv:2312.04511, ICML 2024) already captures inter-call latency via DAG parallelism without correctness risk. The negative result is actionable: the cheap baseline (truncate-never-redo at N=512, or rely on existing incremental-prefill) already captures the available latency without detector/redo apparatus. Do not build.
```
